   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Visions
YIFoS (Youth  Interfaith  Forum  on  Sexuality)  is  an  organisation  consisting  of  young  people from  diverse  religions  aiming  to  build  positive  discourse  between  sexuality  and  faith. In Indonesia  where  religion  and  faith  areoften  misused  to legitimate discrimination regarding gender  and  sexuality, YIFOS  has  been  consistently promoting justice and equality by initiating constructive  dialogue, social  and  spiritual reflection, and reinterpreting religious texts withmore progressive approach. YIFoS is also active in encouraging religious, social and political  institutions  to  set  rules  and  policy  that  respectpeople  with  diverse  genders  and sexualities  as  well  as  building  network  with  individualsororganisations  which  have  similar
concerns.

Activity and Accomplishment
Every  year, YIFoS organises the Queer Camp/Young Queer Faith  and Sexuality Camp. It is a safe space for participants coming from various places in Indonesia to learn allabout sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, and
sexual characteristic (SOGIESC) and collaborate on topics about progressive interpretations in religion that accept and accommodate diversity.

In  March  2019, YIFOS achieved an important breakthrough through successfully organising an expert forum called Religion and Diverse Sexuality Symposium where religious scholars, clerics and thinkers from various religions were invited and encouraged to present their papers or articles focusing on diversity in context  of religions and sexuality. At least, twenty papers or articles have been written, presented and are now in progress to publish.

Geographical Coverage
In terms of geographical coverage, YIFoS has strong commitment to engage young people from various places in Indonesia. Technically speaking, YIFoS#  organisational  structure consists of a diverse committee from West Java, Central  Java, East  Java, and Eastern Indonesia. Furthermore, in every activity or event, YIFoS  always  involvepeople, either as participant, organiser or  speaker, from various regions. Thus YIFoS has strong network with other organisations and individuals around archipelago.</narrative>
